WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.135 --> 00:00:02.009
SPEAKER: Let me show
you how to upload a file

00:00:02.009 --> 00:00:03.640
to cloud storage with Fog.

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:06.330
Fog is a cloud services
library for Ruby.

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:07.990
To use it with Google
Cloud Platform,

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:11.140
you'll use the Fog Google gem.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:13.130
The gem supports several
ways to authenticate.

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:17.720
I've stored my GCP
credentials an a .Fog file.

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:19.470
Here's the code I used
to upload the file.

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:20.318
First, I connect.

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:31.550
Now, add a bucket.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:33.980
Remember, bucket
names must be unique.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:35.482
I'm using DNS-based naming.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.000
Now, I open the file
and upload the file

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.372
using the put object method.

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:56.580
That's it.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:58.830
To learn more about GCP
or Fog, look at the links

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:00.760
in the video description.

